        'While phone theft during travel is plausible under a travel policy, the claim processing timeline is highly unusual: submission, assignment, rejection, and override all occurred within 2 minutes. This compressed decision cycle and the override of a rapid rejection warrant investigation into whether proper claim verification procedures were followed. Additionally, the incident date is unknown despite the claimant stating it occurred ''last week,'' which should be clarified. Documentation supporting the theft (police report, carrier statement, proof of ownership) should be verified.',
